we've talked before about the problem  that we have in political discourse when  one side doesn't accept facts it is a  real impediment to being able to make  progress and have good-faith debate  about any issue that we find important  and we're seeing that now front and  center with the Ukraine Fiasco where  only 40 percent of Republicans 40  percent of Republicans believe that  Donald Trump spoke to the Ukrainian  president about Joe Biden on the phone  remember Donald Trump is admitted to  this that bogus transcript which was  actually a memo sort of a truncated  summary of the call includes a  discussion of Joe Biden between Donald  Trump and the Ukrainian president  Ukrainian presidents so let's take a  step back and think about opinion versus  fact if you poll people about something  like their opinion on gay marriage it is  far more reasonable that you would have  very different perspectives from  Democrats Republicans and independents  now for me I think that the opinion on  gay marriage there's only one right  opinion on gay marriage but okay this is  a matter of opinion and you would expect  more difference in people's opinion on  gay marriage but when Monmouth  University Polling Institute asked  people do you believe that Donald Trump  spoke about Joe Biden on that phone call  with the Ukrainian president almost all  Democrats believed that that is  something that was discussed about 60%  of independents believed that it was  something that was discussed but only  40% of Republicans believed it Donald  Trump admitted that they discussed this  on the call not only did Trump admit it  when asked but the truncated transcript  their memo that the White House released  also includes the mention of Biden so  what do we do what do we do when one  side won't even accept inconvenient but  verified facts that their own leader  gives to them now of course there's the  separate question of whether Donald  Trump extorted or tried to extort  Ukraine and there's lots of other  questions but Trump admitted that they  spoke about Biden and 60% of Republicans  either don't believe it or don't know  now there are some possible questions  about this poll it was conducted during  a period mostly after the transcript or  memo was released but there was one  polling day in there that was before it  was released some people may just not  have seen the new  about that yet but the trend is very  clear if they don't like the facts they  pretend they don't exist and this makes  it difficult or even impossible to  advance serious conversations about what  has to be done it's similar with climate  change where there are real serious  conversations about what policies should  we have what degree of government  involvement should there be in climate  change in dealing with that what about  personal responsibility when dealing  with climate change whatever question  you want to talk about we can't even get  on the same page about what the facts  are because some large portion of the  American right-wing just refuses to  accept the facts on climate change we  can't possibly fix anything or even  discuss it in good faith if one side  doesn't accept the facts and sadly this  is how I end up back at we need to get  around them to win we don't we can't try  to win with them a conversation about  how to proceed with Trump or about the  economy or about who to vote for in 2020  or about tariffs these conversations are  pointless as ways to engage with people  about making change in 2020 if they  won't even accept basic facts including  ones that their Dear Leader gives them  the short answer is you can't  and you shouldn't and we don't need to  as the upside I don't want to be a  broken record again but half the country  doesn't vote meaning you don't have to  go out and find people and convince them  that voting for Trump is a bad idea  that's not necessary to win this you  just need to find people who are already  on our side and just explain to them the  importance of voting and that is much  easier to do it's still not easy I've  met people who don't vote and it's it's  not easy to convince them that they  should be voting but it is easier than  convincing someone who won't even  believe Trump when Trump says we talked  about Joe Biden on the Ukrainian  president phone call and I don't even  think that we should bother doing it
 

